hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"716","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""When a fly falls into the vessel of any one of you, he should immerse it, for indeed in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure (healing)."""
"717","It is narrated from Muslim that he asked Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) about drinking while standing: and people drank while standing."
"718","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), only two things—dates and water—were our food."
"719","It is narrated from Dawud bin Farahij that he heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate in this manner."
"720","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I was among the people of Suffah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Ajwa dates to us, and they were placed before us. Due to hunger, we began to eat two dates at a time. When any one of us combined two dates and ate them, he would say to his companion: I have combined two dates, so you also combine (yours)."
"721","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man accepted Islam while he used to eat excessively. When he accepted Islam, he began to eat less. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A disbeliever eats with seven intestines, whereas a believer eats with one intestine."""
"722","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, whereas the believer eats in one intestine."""
"723","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) never found fault with food; if he liked it, he ate it, and if he disliked it, he left it."
"724","Abu Yahya, the freed slave of Ja'dah, narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to this."
"725","Abul-Ma'arik Bahjaheemi narrated: I asked Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) about drinking while standing. He said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I was holding the camel’s rein in my hand while he (peace be upon him) was riding it, my feet were on its shoulders. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for a drink and drank it, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) gave it to such and such person who was on his right side, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) left me at that place. So if you do not see others being given preference over me after me, then do not consider it blameworthy. Abul-Ma'arik said: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: Whoever is in debt and is well-off, yet does not pay it, then he is like one who eats what is forbidden."
"726","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats soil, he assists in destroying himself."""
"727","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Use olive oil and make it a dish, for it is blessed."""
"728","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""When any of you eats, let him eat with his right hand and drink with his right hand, for indeed Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."""
"729","Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Umar narrates from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"730","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): Seven mastigures were presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a vessel, and ghee was poured over them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I abstain from it, so you eat it."""
"731","Lady Umm Ayub (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed as a guest with us, so we prepared food for him. There was a (pungent-smelling) vegetable in it. When we presented it to him, he disliked it and said: ""Eat it, for I am not like you among you. I fear that I might cause discomfort to (Gabriel, peace be upon him) who is with me."""
"732","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade (the use of) oil-coated jars, vessels made from gourds, and pitch-coated vessels."
"733","It is narrated from Abu Nazrah that a woman asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): How did you prepare nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? She replied: We used to soak dates for him at night, and he would drink it the next morning."
"734","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When any of you eats food, he should not clean his hand until he has licked it or had it licked."""
